{"repositoryId":760223932,"availability":"available","full":"hubertsiuzdak/snac","name":"snac","description":"Multi-Scale Neural Audio Codec (SNAC) compresses audio into discrete codes at a low bitrate","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":776,"forks":45,"created":"2024-02-20T02:33:25Z","updated":"2024-11-19T12:21:57Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://hubertsiuzdak.github.io/snac/","topics":["audio","audio-codec","deep-learning"],"demo":"https://hubertsiuzdak.github.io/snac/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-18T22:42:17.448Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-18T22:42:17.448Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-18T22:42:17.448Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T13:37:35.972Z","stars":776,"forks":46},{"at":"2026-10-18T22:42:17.448Z","stars":776,"forks":45}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Multi-Scale Neural Audio Codec (SNAC) compresses audio into discrete codes at a low bitrate. For more information, read the paper:","SNAC encodes audio into hierarchical tokens similarly to SoundStream, EnCodec, and DAC (see the image on the left). However, SNAC introduces a simple change where coarse tokens are sampled less frequently, covering a broader time span (see the image on the right).","This can not only save on bitrate, but more importantly this might be very useful for language modeling approaches to audio generation. E.g. with coarse tokens of 10 Hz and a context window of 2048 you can effectively model a consistent structure of an audio track for 3 minutes."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/hubertsiuzdak/snac/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"5b79c5eff914a3ac2bc429fdc0dcef3b072646be5390fffdd89092f386d38b1e","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:36.107Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T13:37:36.107Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Multi-Scale Neural Audio Codec (SNAC) compresses audio into discrete codes at a low bitrate. For more information, read the